WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
- Ken and I both listen
carefully on our shows,

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.270
The Masked Singer and The Voice,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.410
but how well can we identify the sounds

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.370
made by everyday objects?

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.350
Probably not well,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.930
I'm not great at this.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.020
It's time to find out with
the game we first played

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.600
with Emily Blunt for her movie,

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.860
A Quiet Place.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.010
We liked it so much.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.870
My producers love humiliating me.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.070
So we figured what the hell,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.085
let's do it again.

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:22.070
(audience laughing)

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.713
This is "A Quiet Case".

00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:25.467
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:29.152
♪ A quiet case ♪

00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:30.364
♪ Shh ♪

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:31.873
(hosts laughing)

00:00:31.873 --> 00:00:32.996
- Jessie!

00:00:32.996 --> 00:00:33.865
- [Jessie] It's an invisible case!

00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:34.930
- It's quiet, it's quiet.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:35.763
We're fun,

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:36.596
we're clever.

00:00:36.596 --> 00:00:37.429
(Ken laughing)

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:38.360
- First, we need a host though.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.500
And for that, we have one of the best,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.674
our friend, Matt Iseman everybody!

00:00:42.674 --> 00:00:45.194
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.194 --> 00:00:47.777
(upbeat music)

00:00:50.389 --> 00:00:52.600
- I love this bromance!

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.450
Okay, tell us how the game works.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.760
- So this is "A Quiet Case".

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.090
You'll get to choose a
case, I will bring it out.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.100
There are microphones here.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.260
I will use the item inside.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.950
When you think you know what it is,

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.783
buzz in and answer.

00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:05.570
If you get it right, you get the point.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.060
If not, your opponent can steal.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.030
- Okay, I like that you're
already thinking I'm gonna win.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.663
Okay, I like it. Project
it! Project it! Okay.

00:01:13.663 --> 00:01:15.180
- This is so authoritarian,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.240
can you repeat it again for me please?

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.110
- So one more time, choose a case.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.360
Remember the steals are allowed.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.080
Now, Ken, you are playing

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.368
for the men in the audience.

00:01:23.368 --> 00:01:24.201
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:01:24.201 --> 00:01:25.440
- What's up?

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.273
What's up?

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.522
Playing for the men!

00:01:28.522 --> 00:01:30.613
- And Kelly's playing for the ladies!

00:01:30.613 --> 00:01:32.280
- Exactly! Exactly!

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:35.120
- We're in trouble, Ken.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.430
Alright Kelly, it's your house,

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.930
